          "text": "Patient-reported right lower leg symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Small red patch on the right shin noticed yesterday morning, with increased redness and spread a little down and around the side over approximately 24–36 hours. Local warmth, mild tenderness to palpation, and tight feeling on standing. Initially no itch; now mild itch at the edges only. No pus or obvious wound reported. Able to weight bear and walk; pain approximately 3/10 and not out of proportion."
      }
